{"title":"2012 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Mrs. Olson begins a journey at the intersection of Avenue <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and First Street in\nthe upper left on the attached map. She ends her journey at one of the Starbucks on \nAvenue <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />. There is a Starbucks on Avenue <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> at every intersection from First Street\nthrough Sixth Street! If Mrs. Olson walks only East and South, how many different\npaths to a Starbucks on Avenue <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> can she take? Note that Mrs. Olson may pass one\nStarbucks on her way to another Starbucks farther to the East.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/b/01bb6c3b0308134e000fef05ec2fe00371024e04.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(300,100); path R=((0,0)--(0,1)--(2,1)--(2,0)--cycle); for(int rw=0;rw&lt;5;++rw){ for (int cl=0;cl&lt;7;++cl){ filldraw(shift(3*cl,2*rw)*R,green);} }  MP(&quot;Avenue \\: D&quot;,(12,1+.5),E); MP(&quot;Avenue \\: C&quot;,(12,3+.5),E); MP(&quot;Avenue \\: B&quot;,(0,5+.5),E); MP(&quot;Avenue \\: A&quot;,(0,7+.5),E); MP(90,&quot;1st\\: Street&quot;,(3-.5,0),N); MP(90,&quot;2cnd\\: Street&quot;,(6-.5,0),N); MP(90,&quot;3rd\\: Street&quot;,(9-.5,0),N); MP(90,&quot;4th\\: Street&quot;,(12-.5,4),N); MP(90,&quot;5th\\: Street&quot;,(15-.5,4),N); MP(90,&quot;6th\\: Street&quot;,(18-.5,4),N);  [/asy]\" width=\"372\" height=\"168\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/b/4bb4795bbf9125d08b3ddc9fbe238166da3bb450.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$126$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_UNCO_Math_Contest_II\" title=\"2012 UNCO Math Contest II\">2012 UNCO Math Contest II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems\" title=\"2012 UNCO Math Contest II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2012 UNCO Math Contest II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\